    fdo:context "Found in the foundations of the chancel of St Mary's, Gowran (SMR KK020-060006-), demolished in 1827; the inscription was first noticed in 1849. Now on site in the rebuilt chancel. Described in OG(H)AM entry I-KIK-007." ;
    dct:type <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2016147> ;
    dct:subject <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q70892361> ;
    dct:subject <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1048392> ;
    fdo:documentationPurpose "Photogrammetric documentation of an ogham stone (Ogham in 3D, Kilkenny 3D)." ;
    fdo:overallCondition "The inscription is in generally good condition but chipped in places (OG(H)AM I-KIK-007)." ;
    fdo:acquisitionMethod "Photogrammetry (structure from motion) with KIRI Engine" ;
    fdo:acquisitionImagesCount "111" ;
    dct:provenance "Scan quality is limited by poor lighting at the site (uploader's note); published on Sketchfab. For this FDO the model was re-oriented in Blender (180 degrees about the horizontal axis towards the preview camera, i.e. Euler XYZ 180,0,-90) so that the stone stands upright; the Sketchfab original is unchanged."  .

